{%- doc -%}
  Renders the unit price, including its measurement.

  @param {object} price - The unit price (money or string).
  @param {object} measurement - The unit_price_measurement object.

  @example
  {% render 'unit-price', price: variant.unit_price, measurement: variant.unit_price_measurement %}

  @example
  {% render 'unit-price', price: line_item.unit_price | money_with_currency, measurement: line_item.unit_price_measurement }
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Senseless (22 Sep 2026): renders NOTHING, by founder decision. Unit pricing is set on the
  variants (scripts/set-unit-pricing.py: per kg / per litre / per item) so the Google & YouTube
  feed can send unit_pricing_measure to Merchant Center. It is deliberately not shown on the site.
  Every theme caller (price.liquid for product cards / search / collection grids, and
  cart-products.liquid) renders through this snippet, so this one change hides it everywhere.
  To show it again, set ss_show_unit_price to true (and restore the cart block in cart-products.liquid).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ss_show_unit_price = false -%}
{%- if ss_show_unit_price -%}
<small class="unit-price">
  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'accessibility.unit_price' | t }}</span>
  {{ price | unit_price_with_measurement: measurement }}
</small>
{%- endif -%}
